# Agent-Native Rust Guidelines

This codebase strictly enforces the **Agent-Native** standards defined in `AGENTS.md`.

## Mandatory Constraints (Enforced at Compile-Time)

- **Living Wiki File Header**: Every non-test source file must begin with `//!` of at least 100 characters detailing purpose, responsibilities, and architecture (Rule 1).
- **Production Code Limit**: Keep active production code lines under 10,000 characters per file (Rule 2). Decompose into submodules when approaching this threshold. Unit tests in `#[cfg(test)]` do not count against this limit.
- **Documentation Limit**: Keep comments under 4,000 characters per file (Rule 3).
- **Function Physical Limit**: Every function must be under 2,000 characters (~40–50 lines) (Rule 4).
- **Public API Documentation**: All public items must have `///` doc comments with executable doctests (`missing_docs = "deny"`).
- **Panic-Free Production**: Never call `.unwrap()` or `.expect()` in production code. Use typed `Result<T, E>` and `?` operator (`clippy::unwrap_used = "deny"`).

## Verification Workflow
Before reporting any task complete, run:
```bash
cargo check && cargo test --all-targets && cargo test --doc && cargo clippy --all-targets
```
